{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>They provoked Me to jealousy with a no-god.</b> The patriarchs provoked Me with a no-god in the First Temple." "<b>They angered Me with their vanities.</b> In the Second Temple." "<b>And I will provoke them to jealousy with a no-people.</b> In the First Temple, which the Chaldeans destroyed, as it says of them: הֵן אֶרֶץ כַּשְׂדִּים זֶה הָעָם לֹא הָיָה (Isaiah 23:13)." "<b>With a foolish nation I will vex them.</b> That kingdom which destroyed it was not worthy — they had neither script nor language (Gittin 80a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:07.652999906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}